tazlab
======

SliTaz development lab for foreign GNU/Linux hosts (Debian, Ubuntu, ...).

POSIX shell, mount + chroot + qemu. No proot, no systemd, no extra
dependencies beyond what every distro already ships.

Install
-------

    sudo make install

Quick start
-----------

    tazlab clone                # clone wok + essential repos
    sudo tazlab setup           # download and extract SliTaz rootfs
    sudo tazlab enter           # mount and enter the chroot

Inside the chroot, on first use:

    tazpkg get-install cookutils

Then back on the host:

    sudo tazlab cook busybox
    sudo tazlab qemu            # test in Qemu

Layout
------

By default everything lives in ~/.slitaz/ on the host:

    chroot/      SliTaz rootfs
    wok/         package recipes (bind-mounted in chroot)
    repos/       cloned HG repos (cookutils, base-files, ...)
    packages/    built .tazpkg files
    cache/       build cache
    log/         build logs
    src/         source tarballs
    iso/         cached SliTaz ISO images

Override via /etc/slitaz/tazlab.conf, ~/.slitaz/tazlab.conf, or
./tazlab.conf (last wins).

Commands
--------

  Chroot:
    setup            Download SliTaz ISO and extract rootfs to chroot
    setup-user [u]   Create an unprivileged user in the chroot
    enter            Mount and enter the chroot as root
    enter-user [u]   Mount and enter as an unprivileged user
    umount           Unmount the chroot
    cook <pkg>       Cook a package inside the chroot
    nuke             Wipe the chroot

  Repos:
    clone            Clone wok + extra repos into ~/.slitaz/repos/
    pull             hg pull -u on all cloned repos
    repos            Show status of each cloned repo
    add-repo <url>   Add an extra HG repo to the list

  Qemu:
    qemu [iso]       Run SliTaz ISO in Qemu (-iso <url> to download)

  Inspect:
    log <pkg>        Show build log (tail -f if building)
    list [filter]    List package recipes in the wok
    search <pat>     Search for a pattern in all receipts
    info <pkg>       Show package receipt

  Maintenance:
    status           Show chroot, wok, packages, repos status
    clean            Clean cache and build logs

Notes
-----

A chroot is not a security boundary. Do not run untrusted package recipes.
